<article class="env-definition" id="05H1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05H1">Definition <span data-tag="05H1">37.58.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. We say $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>finitely presented relative to $S$</em> or <em>of finite presentation relative to $S$</em> if there exists an affine open covering $S = \bigcup V_ i$ and for every $i$ an affine open covering $f^{-1}(V_ i) = \bigcup _ j U_{ij}$ such that $\mathcal{F}(U_{ij})$ is a $\mathcal{O}_ X(U_{ij})$-module of finite presentation relative to $\mathcal{O}_ S(V_ i)$. </p>
</article>